  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phu Luong PC - Post-Typhoon Recovery</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to the impact of the circulation of Typhoon No. 11 (MatMo), heavy rainfall occurred across Thai Nguyen Province from the night of October 6 to October 7, 2025, with rainfall ranging from 250&#x2013;400 mm, and some areas exceeding 500 mm. The heavy rain caused an exceptionally large flood, surpassing historical flood levels, with the Cau River water level rising above Alarm Level 3 during this period. The severe rain and flooding resulted in serious inundation and affected many communes and wards in the province, including Phu Luong Commune.From October 6 to the early morning of October 8, 2025, Phu Luong Commune experienced heavy to very heavy rain, causing landslides, waterlogging, and damage to agriculture, property of residents, and state assets.According to local statistics as of October 15, 2025, many households in the commune were affected and suffered production losses, specifically as follows:Damage to rice, crops, and perennial plants: 395 hectares.Damage to forestry trees: 10.6 hectares.Damage toaquaculture: 14.7 hectares.Livestocklosses: 11,495 animals (chickens, ducks).In addition, many houses and structures were flooded due to the flood, and some householdsexperienced landslides: 723 households were inundated by rain and flood; 10 householdswere affected by landslides with an estimatedlandslide volume of 810 m&#xb3;. Several transportation, irrigation, school, and other infrastructure works were damaged, with estimatedlosses of about 12.7 billion VND.</narrative>
  </description>
